// Pins the refusal the native element release depends on (RV2-DEBT-204).
//
// `emitIndexSet` now frees what an element slot holds before storing over it.
// That is only sound while the value being stored cannot come FROM the slot
// being released — otherwise the release frees the bytes the store is about to
// write back, and the next drop frees them twice.
//
// Nothing local to the emitter enforces that. This does. If the borrow rule is
// ever relaxed to admit a self-assignment through a container, this fixture
// stops being refused, and the release in emitIndexSet needs a guard before
// that relaxation lands.
fn t() {
    let mut xs: string[] = [];
    xs.push("value-long-enough-to-heap-allocate-here");
    xs[0] = xs[0];
}
